      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should probably be documented in a more systematic way.\n\nIterators usually let you remove an element from the collection while iterating but only from the iterator `remove` method (which is why you never do it ; it requires dropping the for loop syntactic sugar).\n\nThis has the following characteristic : you can remove from the arrayset in any way you want the currently iterating NAI or any with a higher index. Conversely if you remove any prior, you\u0027ll handle the same twice.\n\nOne thing that you might want to do for safety is to have a local keeping the last NAI processed and throw ConcurrentModificationException if you find it twice in a row.",
